# Allowlist, not a denylist: everything is excluded, then the Go build inputs
# are added back. A new secret file dropped in the repo root is therefore
# excluded by default rather than requiring this file to be updated.
*

# --- build inputs ---
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd
!cmd/**
!internal
!internal/**
!db
!db/**
# The browser client is a build stage of its own; api/openapi.yaml is not
# needed because src/api/schema.d.ts is generated from it and committed.
!web
!web/**

# --- pared back out of the allowlist above ---
# Tests never run in the image build, and the store tests pull testcontainers.
**/*_test.go
internal/testsupport
# Only db/migrations is embedded (db/embed.go); the sqlc query sources are a
# codegen input, not a runtime one.
db/queries
# Installed and built inside the image, never copied into it. node_modules in
# particular is both enormous and platform-specific to the host that made it.
web/node_modules
web/dist
web/*.tsbuildinfo
# A local `make web` leaves a bundle here. The image builds its own in the web
# stage and copies it over this path, so shipping the local one would only
# risk a stale bundle winning a cache lookup.
internal/transport/webui/dist
